cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "StateSpaceSIR: state-space surplus production models fitted by sampling-importance-resampling"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it, along with Romero et al. (2022) for the modelling framework."
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-17"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SW-atlantic-right-whale-assessment/StateSpaceSIR"
abstract: >-
  An R package that fits Bayesian state-space generalized logistic (surplus
  production) models using the sampling-importance-resampling algorithm of
  McAllister et al. (1994). Combines catch series with absolute and relative
  abundance indices, supports multivariate lognormal index likelihoods with
  analytically integrated catchability, and implements four parameterisations of
  a demographic Allee effect. Provides model averaging by Bayes factor, WAIC,
  and plotting and summary methods.
keywords:
  - Bayesian state-space model
  - surplus production
  - sampling-importance-resampling
  - Allee effect
  - depensation
  - stock assessment
  - population dynamics
  - R

